// Voxt's UI strings, addressed by key. Server errors and validation messages live in the
// companion Messages.*.json; a key belongs to exactly one of the two catalogs.
//
// This file is JSONC - '//' comments and trailing commas are allowed. The comments below say
// where each group appears on screen and what it is really about, because a translator
// cannot recover that from the value alone. Keep a new key inside the group it belongs to.
//
// What constrains a translation:
//   {0}, {1}     Placeholders. Every one the English value has must survive; a _Format
//                suffix on the key marks a value that carries them.
//   a|b|c        Plural forms of one key, ordered one|few|many. List only as many as the
//                language actually has - docs/i18n.md has the per-language rules.
//   _Prefix / Target / _Suffix
//                One sentence split around markup - an emphasized span or a child
//                component. Either side may be empty where word order demands it, and any
//                {0} belongs to the _Prefix part.
//   Leading and trailing spaces are load-bearing wherever a fragment is concatenated.
//
// docs/i18n.md carries the rest: the product terms (Place, Public/Private, Join, cookies),
// the politeness register each language uses, and how bs/cnr/hr/sr/max are derived.
